 "relevance_note": "Single-patient case report of a woman with a LAMP2 variant: \"Genetic testing confirmed the diagnosis of Danon disease with a LAMP2 c.733C > T (p.G245*) mutation\".",
 "method_note": "Short case report (one paragraph); read in full and transcribed by hand via a small Python builder in the scratch directory, then spans checked by script. Label 'patient' (rule 5, single unnamed patient). The '25-year-old' age refers to the first presentation 6 years before the report ('6 years ago'), not to onset, diagnosis or last evaluation, so all three age fields are left not reported. 'Non-obstructive' hypertrophic cardiomyopathy recorded as LV outflow tract obstruction excluded in the checklist. NT-proBNP 6625 pg/ml and cTnI 0.42 ug/l are given as values without being called elevated, so no feature rows. Heart failure is never named (only chest tightness, dyspnea, 'consideration of a decompensation phase' and heart transplantation), so the heart-failure checklist item is not reported. Variant type not recorded: the paper calls it only a 'mutation'; no zygosity, parental testing or transcript stated. No contradictions found. Supplementary data and figures not available in the text.",
